   "ResearcherNotesUnit": "AL, Jun 2025: Initially marked terminal as operating based on several reports, satellite imagery, and videos by INOXCVA, but I terminal's commissioning date is sketchy. IGU 2025 said project was still under construction and was expected to go online in 2025; however, other sources seem to imply that terminal is already operating (calling it a success). I finally went for construction based on group discussion and news segment from 2025 saying it was about to be operational but there seem to be dredging issues that prevent it from becoming operational. GC, Sep 2024: It's hard to tell how close this project is to commissioning. Company website shows the terminal and associated power plant to still be under construction. The associated power plant was being tested as of November 2023 and slated to run on diesel until the LNG terminal could be completed: https://pointville.ag/testing-of-new-lng-power-plant-underway/ A June 2024 article in the Antigua Observer indicated that the plant would be \"commissioned later this year on gas,\" implying that the LNG terminal would come online in 2024, but this information feels pretty sketchy: https://antiguaobserver.com/apua-reintroduces-transparent-fuel-variation-charge-for-a-sustainable-future/  Gregor, July 2023: A February 2023 news article showed the power plant associated with this proposed LNG terminal to be on track for a July 2023 commissioning date - https://antigua.news/2023/02/14/new-lng-power-plant-on-target/ -  but I can't find proof that construction of the terminal itself is underway, and the owner (Eagle LNG) has said they'll supply it from the yet-to-be-built Eagle LNG Export Terminal in Florida, so I'm leaving this in Proposed status for now.",
